/E (In the 1970s and early 1980s, the networking world was a bit of a mess. Companies like IBM developed their own systems and protocols, meaning that their machines would only communicate with other IBM machines. This practice, called vendor lock-in, made it difficult for different brands to interact with one another.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [9]
>>
