/P 172 0 R
/E (To address this problem, the International Organization for Standardization \(ISO\) developed the OSI \(Open Systems Interconnection\) model in the early 1980s. The goal was to create a standard framework that would allow various network technologies to communicate with each other, regardless of their manufacturer. The OSI model broke down the complexities of network communication into 7 distinct layers, each with specific functions.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
220 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 172 0 R
